# AI Academy Mobile — Design System (pointer)

Before changing UI, read the canonical documents — this rule does not restate them:

| Need | Read |
|---|---|
| Method for turning a frame into code, states the frame omits, copy, visual QA, checklist | `docs/design-system/FIGMA_TO_FLUTTER.md` (start here) |
| Three value tiers, colour, typography (shipped ~15% below Figma), spacing spine 393/16/361/329/480, icons, shadows | `docs/design-system/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md` |
| Reusable widgets, reuse order, loading/empty/error trio, accessibility | `docs/design-system/COMPONENT_PATTERNS.md` |
| Screen skeleton and documented exceptions | `docs/design-system/SCREEN_PATTERNS.md` |

Non-negotiables those documents expand on: Figma "App UI" is the visual authority, existing UI is only implementation context; no literal without a recorded measurement; never invent a state; a visual change is verified rendered, or the gap is stated.
